  "dcterms:title": "RTECS - Registry of Toxic Effects of Chemical Substances",
  "dcterms:description": "Records from RTECS (Registry of Toxic Effects of Chemical Substances), a toxicology database of chemical substances with acute toxicity, mutagenicity, irritation, tumorigenic and reproductive-toxicity data indexed by RTECS and CAS numbers. RTECS originated at NIOSH but is now a proprietary commercial product; the data must be purchased and is downloaded from the CCOHS (Canadian Centre for Occupational Health and Safety) FTP portal using licensed credentials.",
